I've toyed around with the idea of a 'shield' skill a lot to encourage
people to consider sword-and-board as a third alternative to the
ubiquitous #twoweapon and the restored-to-prestige two-handed weapon.
But I found that it was just easier and worked better to make shields
that provided enough advantage that it was worth putting them on your
arm and giving up the extra damage bonus of the other two.

Skill slots' problem for me, so far, has been that there's
simultaneously too few and too many of them.  Too few because it
isn't worth advancing anything that isn't your Final Weapon Type(tm)
past 'basic' (and often not even past 'unskilled' even with the to-hit
cap for that I added), and too many because for too many classes, it
only takes a few to max out your Final Weapon Type and then the rest of
them just sit there and get thrown at spells randomly.

I've been inclined to split them off from spell skill simply to make it
more worthwhile to do a minimal amount of early golfbagging (ie. carry a
sling knowing you may dump it later) for classes that would otherwise 
reserve them for utility-spell slots, but i'm still not sure that makes 
them tempting enough.

